<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liqoqo</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Swazi National Council Standing Committee</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Liqoqo is the inner council of senior princes, chiefs and advisers that counsels the king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eswatini">Eswatini</a>. After the death of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sobhuza-ii">Sobhuza II</a> in 1982 it became the dominant power in the kingdom during the regency and was involved in a bitter struggle at court, until the young Mswati III reduced it to an advisory role in 1986.</p></div>
